# source: SYNTHETIC
# title: Server hangs up an answered call: the BYE it sends (From/To swapped, our tag, reachable Via, CSeq 2 BYE)
# verdict: MATCH
# basis: README / main.go byeTo: an inbound call's BYE has From = the To we were sent, with our tag

>>> send
INVITE sip:9901@{{SRV}} SIP/2.0
Via: SIP/2.0/UDP {{ST}};branch=z9hG4bKinv1
From: <sip:8001@{{ST}}>;tag=st-call-1
To: <sip:9901@{{SRV}}>
Call-ID: call-1
CSeq: 1 INVITE
Contact: <sip:8001@{{ST}}>
Content-Type: application/sdp
Max-Forwards: 70

v=0
o=- 0 0 IN IP4 {{STIP}}
s=-
c=IN IP4 {{STIP}}
t=0 0
m=audio {{RTP}} RTP/AVP 97 8 0 18 9 102 103 101
a=rtpmap:97 PCM/16000
a=rtpmap:8 PCMA/8000
a=rtpmap:0 PCMU/8000
a=rtpmap:18 G729/8000
a=rtpmap:9 G722/8000
a=rtpmap:102 G722/16000
a=rtpmap:103 PCM/8000
a=rtpmap:101 telephone-event/8000
m=video 20000 RTP/AVP 96
a=rtpmap:96 H264/90000
.
>>> recv
>>> answer
>>> recv
>>> send
ACK sip:9901@{{SRV}} SIP/2.0
Via: SIP/2.0/UDP {{ST}};branch=z9hG4bKack1
From: <sip:8001@{{ST}}>;tag=st-call-1
To: <sip:9901@{{SRV}}>
Call-ID: call-1
CSeq: 1 ACK
Max-Forwards: 70
.
>>> hangup
>>> recv
>>> state
